# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the test suite.
#
# Mesa's llvmpipe (the software OpenGL driver used on machines without a GPU,
# including CI) has a shutdown race entirely inside libgallium: its rasteriser
# worker threads can still be taking a mutex while eglDestroyContext() destroys
# it. No rei-wm memory is involved. Races whose stacks are in that library are
# ignored; races in rei-wm's own code are still reported.
race:libgallium

# Pango loads fonts on its own background thread ("[pango] fontconfig") and hands
# work to the calling thread through glib queues and fontconfig structures. glib's
# mutexes are futex based and invisible to ThreadSanitizer, so a correctly
# synchronised hand-off is reported as a race, with every frame inside these
# libraries. rei-wm only calls Pango from the event thread and shares none of its
# own data with that thread.
race:libglib
race:libfontconfig
race:libpango
race:libpangocairo
race:libcairo
